# ./bench profile pair for catalog-int4-vs-int8-android.cells: the Qwen3-1.7B
# INT8 (dynamic_wi8_afp32) file vs the dynamic wi4b32 file on the GPU backend,
# litert_lm_advanced_main 128x256 at max_num_tokens 1024 — one control + one
# --enable_profiling run each, so the weight-GEMV op time per decode step can be
# set against the static weight bytes per token of each file (the whole-model
# rate pair is confounded by the wi4b32 build's fused GPU graph; the per-op
# GEMV family is not). Run after the matrix, same campaign name:
#
#   BENCH_ANDROID_SERIAL=RFGL80R6A6H BENCH_CPU_MASK= ./bench profile matrices/catalog-int4-vs-int8-android-profile.cells --campaign <date>-catalog-int4-vs-int8-s26
